WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.759
There's a lot of entrepreneurs that message
me and say, "Pat, one day I'm running a billion

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:06.970
dollar company."

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:09.360
And I'll send a message back and say, "How?"

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.059
And they say, "That's why I need your help,
to build a billion dollar company."

00:00:12.059 --> 00:00:16.620
You see, saying that statement is exciting
because you know, it's very similar when we're

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.310
excited and we're inspired, we watch a video,
we watch a movie, maybe a documentary and

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.640
say, "I'm going to be the next this, I'm going
to be the next.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.530
. . I'm going to build a billion-dollar company.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.260
Then comes the how-to, the logic later.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.260
Then we're stuck.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:29.260
And then we give up.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.350
It's like, it's important you need the emotion,
it's like when you fall in love with a girl

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:34.829
and you say, I love you so much.

00:00:34.829 --> 00:00:35.829
This is great!

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:41.280
And then the emotion leads to sex and then
you have a baby, then you say, how do I raise

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.280
this kid?

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.280
Well, that's the real work.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:44.280
The same exact principle.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.910
I'm going to build a billion dollar company.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:47.460
How am I going to build this company?

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.180
So, that's one thing to keep in mind.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.260
There's nothing wrong with that.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:52.520
We need more inspiration, more motivation.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.020
But today I'm going to give you a little bit
of logic to be thinking about.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:01.100
First of all, before I build a billion dollar
company, I got to build a million dollar business.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.810
And how do I get to a million dollar business?

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:03.890
How do I get to a 10 million dollar?

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:08.270
And how many companies are there that are
really doing this, and how do they think?

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:15.439
I can tell you for myself, I went from starting
the company, and from scratch, nothing, 100%

00:01:15.439 --> 00:01:16.439
my savings.

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:17.689
Didn't get a loan from anybody.

00:01:17.689 --> 00:01:18.979
Didn't go raise capital.

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:19.979
Nothing.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:22.950
100% all my savings was put into it.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.759
Every single penny I had was put into the
business.

00:01:25.759 --> 00:01:29.740
And we took that from there now to, you know,
we're getting offers of $100 million for the

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:30.740
company.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:32.969
And I went from zero to $100 million in seven
years.

00:01:32.969 --> 00:01:36.479
And so, I'm going to talk about some of those
principles for you to be thinking about.

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:42.049
Then at the same time, I want you to be seeing
this here on how many billion dollar companies

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:43.049
are out there.

00:01:43.049 --> 00:01:44.049
So here's what it is.

00:01:44.049 --> 00:01:49.380
There are 30 million companies in America,
that are registered in America, 30 million

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.380
companies.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.859
96% of them gross less than a million a year.

00:01:53.859 --> 00:01:54.939
Keep that in mind.

00:01:54.939 --> 00:01:58.250
96% of them do less than a million dollars
per year.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.869
Only 4% do more than a million dollars per
year.

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:08.090
That's 1.2 million companies do a million
dollar a year or more in revenue.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.230
.4% which is 120,000 companies do more than
10 million.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:18.129
Out of 30 million, only 120,000 do over 10
million dollars a year in revenue.

00:02:18.129 --> 00:02:20.360
Let me explain to you what that means.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:25.950
Out of all the people in America, to make
six figures, you're in the 20th percentile.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.540
20% of Americans household make a six figure
income.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:37.909
Now, the 1% number, "I want to be a one-percenter,"
- a one-percenter is shy of $400,000 a year

00:02:37.909 --> 00:02:38.909
income.

00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:45.129
We're talking about .4% of companies do $10
million or more per year.

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:51.280
Then .0006, that's 18,000 companies do more
than 50 million.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.280
This is like a prime.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:53.439
If you're here, you're good.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:56.560
If you get over 10 million, you have respect
now from peers.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.849
50 million, there's only 18,000.

00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:05.590
If you want to get to .00009%, 2500 companies
do more than 500 million dollars of revenue

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:06.590
per year.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.310
And then you have the ultimate Fortune 500
companies.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:13.680
That's .00002%, you're doing more than 5 billion
per year.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.750
And this is the top 10 currently right now
of Fortune 500 companies.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:23.459
#10 is AT&amp;T, then it's Ford, then GM, then
CVS Health, the United Healthcare Group, then

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:29.599
McKessan, then Berkshire Hathaway, then it's
Apple, then it's Exxon, then Wal-Mart, number

00:03:29.599 --> 00:03:35.040
one, in America, 2.2 million employees in
the world, I think 1.6 million in America

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.230
is what they have.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.510
So, now, what is the biggest difference between
these guys [more than one million] and these

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.330
guys [less than one million]?

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:43.239
The majority's under a million.

00:03:43.239 --> 00:03:45.250
How do I even get to a million dollar business?

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.749
What's the difference?

00:03:46.749 --> 00:03:48.200
What's the difference between these guys [more
than 10 million and more than 1 million] , because

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.010
that's 4% and that's .4%.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.010
What is that?

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:52.010
That's what we're going to talk about.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.010
So first things first.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:56.219
When I had a group of these entrepreneurs
that flew in a couple of weeks ago from all

00:03:56.219 --> 00:03:59.370
over the world, they came from all over the
world, they won the contest for us getting

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:03.940
to 100,000 subs, and I'm, you know, most likely
when we get to a quarter million subs we'll

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:08.550
put the same contest again for people to fly
in and we'll do the same structure, maybe

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.080
at a different place.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:13.540
But we went for hours after hours dissecting
businesses.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:17.660
And the first question I asked all the entrepreneurs
was the one thing that most people don't have

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:18.660
in mind.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:19.660
The first question I asked.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:23.140
I said, I need you to tell me clearly what
your vision is with your business.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.310
What is your business with your business?

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:30.450
Because in reality, most of them, 96 percenters
don't have any idea what they're doing.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.970
They don't even know why they started a business.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:34.800
It's generally just pure excitement, enthusiasm.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:35.800
I hate my boss.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:36.960
I hate my job.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.370
I don't ever want to work for anybody else.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:39.370
I want to start a business.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:41.580
That's pretty much how it starts, right?

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.940
But if you want to get to the higher level
and build a billion dollar company or something

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:48.470
that maybe one day will be valued at a billion
dollar company, you need to be very clear

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:49.470
about what you want.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.310
What is your vision?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.500
What is your long-term vision?

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:53.790
What are we doing?

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.090
What are we doing five years from now?

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.190
What are we doing 10 years from now?

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.190
What do you want to be?

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.190
Who do you want to be?

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:59.190
Where do you want to be?

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.530
Is it clear to you?

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.500
Do you know exactly where you're going?

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:03.770
Do you know exactly what you want to do?

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:08.320
I did a video last week and it was called
the biggest mistake marketers make.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:12.669
And in this video, the biggest mistake marketers
make, I explained how everybody wants everybody

00:05:12.669 --> 00:05:14.250
to be their customers.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.199
They want to appeal to every single person.

00:05:16.199 --> 00:05:18.250
If you haven't watched it, you've got to watch
this video.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:22.440
But the ones that do very well, they understand
exactly what clear vision they have, who's

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.759
their customer and they stay in that lane
the entire time.

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:28.020
So the first thing I will tell you to build
a big company is you've got to have a vision.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:32.599
I remember the night when we had a meeting,
September 23, everybody talks about it all

00:05:32.599 --> 00:05:33.800
the time.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:38.820
And I pulled in the agents and I told them,
we are starting a new company.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.920
This is the first thing I told everybody that
night.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.272
Till today, everyone talks about it.

00:05:42.272 --> 00:05:47.300
I got up, and I said, "There's a 90% chance
we're going out of business within six months."

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.080
That was my opening line.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.080
This is recorded.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.330
There's a 90% chance we're going out of business.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:53.790
My wife was standing in the back.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.490
We've just been married for three months.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:57.500
My father's telling me, "Don't do it!"

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:02.229
I said, "I'm putting every single dime I've
ever worked for and saved into this deal.

00:06:02.229 --> 00:06:03.470
100% of it.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:06.280
Because I'm crystal clear of the vision of
what we're gonna be doing."

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:09.539
I don't know what it is, but this is very
crystal clear.

00:06:09.539 --> 00:06:10.710
Here's what we got to do.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:12.000
This is what the industry needs.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.370
This is what we're going to be doing.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.129
And I cast the vision.

00:06:15.129 --> 00:06:18.870
And you can cast the vision and try to motivate,
but if it ain't clear, everyone knows it.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.680
This was a very clear vision.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.430
And we had some that didn't want to take up.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:26.270
And I told them, if you don't want to do anything
like this, I fully understand it because we're

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:28.220
going to have a lot of problems the first
year, two years.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.509
And if you can't handle that, go with a bigger
company.

00:06:30.509 --> 00:06:32.660
If you do want to go with us, mark my words.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:36.840
Every day, every night, we're going to bust
our tails til this thing becomes a reality.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:40.410
There's a certain sense of vision and clarity,
the bigger the business is being built, and

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:44.020
there's something that's deeper than just
let's build a business together.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:45.020
#2: Patience.

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:46.669
You've got to have patience.

00:06:46.669 --> 00:06:50.800
But not patience, because there's two different
types of patience that are sold to people.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.330
There's one patience that's like, "Listen,
be patient.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:53.740
Everything's going to be okay.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:55.500
Be patient, everything's going to be okay.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:56.500
Be patient.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:57.500
You're young.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:58.500
Just be patient.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:06:59.500
Just be patient."

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.500
I don't believe in that.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:01.500
Here's why.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.880
My father, who raised me and I would give
him credit to helping me become a leader - there's

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:08.349
a lot of great men in my life that have impacted
me, many of them.

00:07:08.349 --> 00:07:10.610
And one day I'll do a video and I'll list
them.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:14.050
My father's at the top of the list, but I'll
list these men, not in any order, how they

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:15.120
impacted me.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.310
But my father was always the opposite.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:18.310
My father wasn't saying, "Be patient.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:19.620
Be patient."

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:24.060
My father was, "You're going to be 65 years
old tomorrow, what are you doing?

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.970
How many times do you need to go to the nightclub?

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:26.970
Let's go already!"

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:28.870
I'm like, "Leave me alone, man.

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:30.169
I'm 22 years old!

00:07:30.169 --> 00:07:31.470
I'm 21 years old!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.349
I've got to live it up!"

00:07:33.349 --> 00:07:35.479
How many more girls you want, Pat?

00:07:35.479 --> 00:07:36.889
How many?!

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:38.120
How many more girls do you need?

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:41.130
I mean what do you need to feed your appetite
already?

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.250
Dad, what is wrong with you?

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:44.250
Right?

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:46.719
There is that part where people say, "Just
be patient."

00:07:46.719 --> 00:07:47.719
My dad wasn't that.

00:07:47.719 --> 00:07:48.780
My dad would say, "Let's go.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:49.780
What are we waiting for?

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:50.780
Let's go.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:51.780
Let's go."

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:52.780
And by the way, he was like this since I was
a kid.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.419
He'd wake me up in the morning with water
spraying on my face.

00:07:54.419 --> 00:07:55.949
Let's go wake up!

00:07:55.949 --> 00:07:57.120
And he was never in the military.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.120
Wake up!

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.610
I'm like, Dad, I want to sleep five more minutes.

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:00.610
Oh really?

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:01.610
No problem.

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:02.610
I knew what that meant.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:03.610
He would go and bring the spray.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:04.610
No hesitation [spray, spray, spray].

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:05.610
He would wake me up.

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:06.610
You say, "that's abusive!"

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:09.039
He taught me to be aggressively patient.

00:08:09.039 --> 00:08:12.169
There's a big difference between patience
and aggressively patient.

00:08:12.169 --> 00:08:13.169
What's patience?

00:08:13.169 --> 00:08:14.169
Man, it's going to be okay.

00:08:14.169 --> 00:08:15.169
Just relax.

00:08:15.169 --> 00:08:16.169
Oh, I'm just going to go home.

00:08:16.169 --> 00:08:17.169
I had a bad day today.

00:08:17.169 --> 00:08:18.169
Because I'm going to be patient.

00:08:18.169 --> 00:08:19.650
Oh, it's all good, man.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:20.900
Tomorrow it's another day.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.090
It's another day!

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:23.090
It's another day!

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:25.669
You know how many times you can say it's another
day until you're 80 years old?

00:08:25.669 --> 00:08:26.720
That's about 18,000 times.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.289
I don't know how many days it is.

00:08:28.289 --> 00:08:29.289
However many times.

00:08:29.289 --> 00:08:30.330
Eventually you're 68 years old.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:31.330
What?

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.330
Another day?

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:33.330
It's another day.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:34.330
It's another day.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:35.330
It ain't another day.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:36.330
No, no.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:40.130
It's another day, once I come home I'm so
tired, I don't even make it to my bed.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:41.870
I sleep on the floor.

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:42.870
Yes.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:43.870
You can be patient.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:44.870
That's aggressively patient.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.030
So not just be patient.

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:48.030
Be aggressively patient.

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:50.780
#3, adapting and adjusting.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.250
Here's why.

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.550
On this list I wanted to put product.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:54.890
I didn't put product on here.

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:56.270
Here's why I didn't put product.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:59.200
There's a lot of companies that don't have
the best products in the world that are multi-billion

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.160
dollar companies that we use regularly.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.200
They don't have the best product.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:03.560
How did they do it?

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:04.740
It's adapting.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:06.330
It's adjusting.

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:09.160
It's seeing what the market demands today.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.740
It's seeing what's needed five years from
now.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:15.530
It's knowing as the quarterback you're playing
and all of a sudden you notice it's third

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:18.260
down and three, and you know they know what
they're calling.

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:19.730
They're going to call a blitz.

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:23.530
And you notice that the two linebackers step
up, maybe corners came in a little bit.

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:24.730
Safety backed up.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:27.950
You look at one of your guys and you say hey,
I'm calling audible.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:29.040
You change it up.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.420
Fullback comes to the back.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:33.520
You go to the back, you go this way, and the
next thing you know, this guy opens up.

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:34.520
Boom, he runs.

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:35.520
You throw it.

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:36.520
You've got a touchdown.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:38.200
And you have to call an audible because you
caught something, you read something, right?

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:39.740
You're looking at everything that's moving.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:40.920
Same exact energy.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:44.970
You've got to have if you want to build a
bigger billion dollar company, or even a 100

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:45.970
million dollar company.

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:48.760
You've got to have that eye set to know that
you got to adapt and you've got to adjust.

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:51.520
Point #4, sticking to your philosophy.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.310
Sticking to your philosophy.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.310
